From e82aca98fc9e5583e5d9ea671f4ce57a3e139052 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: harness-bench <noreply@invalid>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 07:19:23 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sandbox): run scenarios against a scripted model with no
 API key

`beacon-sandbox run` drives a real agent session, so every run needs
an API key with credit, and a scenario cannot block egress because the
agent needs the model API.

`run --model scripted` points the agent at a loopback stand-in for the
Messages API instead (new package scriptedmodel). It answers each
request that offers tools with the next step of the scenario's new
optional `script:` field (a list of {tool, input}, placeholders
expanded), then ends the session with a text reply and end_turn.
Side requests (no tools) and /v1/messages/count_tokens are answered
without advancing the script, and a step whose tool the session does
not offer ends the session and is recorded rather than skipped.
The agent still runs every tool and emits its own telemetry, so what
Beacon captures is real; only the agent's decisions are fixed.

In scripted mode no credential is resolved (credentials.SourceScripted
says why the leak check has nothing to search for), the session gets
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, a placeholder ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN, blanked real
credentials and non-essential traffic switched off, and the launch
asks for no egress. Each run writes scripted-model.json and records
scripted_steps_sent in meta.json.

The stand-in runs in this process, so the mode is limited to
--provider local for now; modal and github are refused with an error
naming --provider local. s02-bash-command and s03-file-write gain
scripts. Without --model, or with --model anthropic, behaviour is
unchanged.
