 Three ways to supply the API key, in the order the tool looks: `--modal-secret NAME`,
 `--api-key-command CMD`, or `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`.
 
+### Without an API key
+
+`run --model scripted` replaces the API with a stand-in on `127.0.0.1` that answers from the
+scenario's `script:` — a list of tool calls, each `{tool, input}`, made in order before the session
+ends. Claude Code still runs every tool and emits its own telemetry, so what Beacon captures is
+real; only the agent's decisions are fixed. No key is read, no model call leaves the machine, and
+the agent cannot paraphrase or skip the work. Scenarios without a `script:` are not run.
+
+```yaml
+script:
+  - tool: Bash
+    input: {command: "echo {{canary}} | tee {{sentinel}}", description: Echo the canary}
+```
+
+The stand-in runs inside this process, so for now it needs `--provider local`. Each scripted run
+writes `scripted-model.json`, the list of requests the stand-in answered, and records
+`scripted_steps_sent` in `meta.json`.
+
 ## Testing on Windows
 
 Modal has no Windows machines, so Windows scenarios run on a GitHub Actions Windows runner
